<title>POLAND: POLISH BUDGET DEFICIT AT PLN 1.39 BLN IN FEBRUARY.</title>
<headline>POLISH BUDGET DEFICIT AT PLN 1.39 BLN IN FEBRUARY.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish budget deficit</p>
<p>widened by 1.15 billion zlotys to 1.39 billion zlotys in</p>
<p>February, which accounted for 11.4 percent of the planned 1997</p>
<p>deficit of 12.22 billion zlotys, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p> POLISH BUDGET GAP    Jan-Feb 97	  Jan 97     1997 plan</p>
<p> balance in bln PLN	 1.39		0.23	 12.220</p>
<p> revenue		     15.59		8.10	115.334</p>
<p> expenditure		 16.98		8.33	127.554</p>
<p>NOTE: January figures given as reported last month.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
